        transliteration: "veṇuṁ kvaṇantam aravinda-dalāyatākṣaṁ-\nbarhāvataṁsam asitāmbuda-sundarāṅgam\nkandarpa-koṭi-kamanīya-viśeṣa-śobhaṁ\ngovindam ādi-puruṣaṁ tam ahaṁ bhajāmi",
        translation: "I worship Govinda, the primeval Lord, who is adept in playing on His flute, with blooming lotus-like eyes, head bedecked with peacock feathers, beautiful bodily tint like blue clouds, and whose unique beauty charms millions of Cupids.",
